// Shared API build settings for the app.
//
// The base URL is assembled from a scheme and a host instead of being written
// as one literal because `//` starts a comment in .xcconfig files: a line such
// as `WV_API_BASE_URL = https://api.warrly.com` would silently resolve to
// `https:` and the app would fail at launch.
SLASH = /
WV_API_BASE_URL = $(WV_API_SCHEME):$(SLASH)$(SLASH)$(WV_API_HOST)

// `WV_API_BASE_URL` reaches the app through the generated Info.plist key
// `WVAPIBaseURL`; `App/Info.plist` is generated from project.yml — never edit
// it by hand. `BaseURLResolver` in WarrlyKit reads the key at runtime and
// crashes with a readable message if it is missing or malformed.
//
// Build overrides still work:
//   xcodebuild ... WV_API_BASE_URL=https://staging.warrly.com
// and the launch-environment override `WV_BASE_URL` wins over both.

// ── AdMob banner unit ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Reaches the app through the generated Info.plist key `GADBannerUnitID`
// (`AdsConfig` in App/Ads/AdsConfig.swift). Per configuration, because the
// value is a policy boundary, not a preference:
//
//   Debug   → Google's published TEST banner unit. Every impression is a test
//             impression: no revenue, and tapping it cannot be a policy
//             violation.
//   Release → Warrly's real banner unit.
//
// The publisher id (pub-1055054650162014) is SHARED with the owner's other iOS
// app, so a live ad clicked in this app would hurt that one too.
//
// No `//` anywhere in these values — in an .xcconfig that starts a comment and
// would truncate the id (if a future unit id ever contains a double slash, use
// the SLASH trick above). The value itself lives in Debug.xcconfig /
// Release.xcconfig, like WV_API_SCHEME and WV_API_HOST.
